window.DayNotes=[{q:"“A dashboard should help you see the operation. It should never become a substitute for seeing the operation.”",id:"note-01-dashboard",d:"20 September 2026",iso:"2026-09-20",img:"/media/notes/en/01-dashboard.jpg?v=1522bf07a5"},{q:"“If a problem needs the same reminder every day, the reminder is not the system.”",id:"note-02-reminder",d:"20 September 2026",iso:"2026-09-20",img:"/media/notes/en/02-reminder.jpg?v=08615b2278"},{q:"“Ownership begins where the sentence ‘someone should’ ends.”",id:"note-03-ownership",d:"20 September 2026",iso:"2026-09-20",img:"/media/notes/en/03-ownership.jpg?v=83d0de3890"},{q:"“The night shift exposes weak processes because fewer people are available to hide them.”",id:"note-04-night-shift",d:"20 September 2026",iso:"2026-09-20",img:"/media/notes/en/04-night-shift.jpg?v=388974fc20"},{q:"“In Excel, a mistake is a number. On the ramp, it has an address.”",id:"note-01-excel",d:"4 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-04",img:"/media/notes/en/01-excel.jpg?v=3f72f75792"},{q:"“A KPI tells you where to look. It does not tell you by itself what happened.”",id:"note-02-kpi",d:"4 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-04",img:"/media/notes/en/02-kpi.jpg?v=05465f9f91"},{q:"“If you manage only the number, you can punish the wrong person.”",id:"note-03-the-number",d:"4 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-04",img:"/media/notes/en/03-the-number.jpg?v=b8734465b6"},{q:"“An analysis padded to look good is more dangerous than an incomplete analysis that admits its own limit.”",id:"note-04-analysis",d:"4 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-04",img:"/media/notes/en/04-analysis.jpg?v=02d918e26f"},{q:"“Do not cling to the chair you used to have. Take with you what you learned while sitting in it.”",id:"note-05-the-chair",d:"4 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-04",img:"/media/notes/en/05-the-chair.jpg?v=7dd10f6cc5"},{q:"“The person doing the work should not have to search for the information. The information should be where they expect it.”",id:"note-06-information",d:"4 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-04",img:"/media/notes/en/06-information.jpg?v=7f297cfb8b"},{q:"“I have not become less flexible. I have become less willing to let flexibility replace the system.”",id:"note-07-flexibility",d:"4 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-04",img:"/media/notes/en/07-flexibility.jpg?v=bca2d775de"},{q:"“Authority without a title is not earned by behaving as if you had a title. It is earned by being useful.”",id:"note-08-authority",d:"4 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-04",img:"/media/notes/en/08-authority.jpg?v=82788f3bc7"},{q:"“Initiative and authority are two different things.”",id:"note-09-initiative",d:"4 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-04",img:"/media/notes/en/09-initiative.jpg?v=ac6b5b686f"},{q:"“Leadership is not becoming the person without whom nothing works. Leadership is helping things work even when you are not there.”",id:"note-10-leadership",d:"4 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-04",img:"/media/notes/en/10-leadership.jpg?v=a2f90ccb14"},{q:"“During the day, management sees the activity. At night, you see the traces the activity has left behind.”",id:"note-11-traces",d:"4 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-04",img:"/media/notes/en/11-traces.jpg?v=d16376dd87"},{q:"“A problem that does not make it into the handover does not stop existing. It just becomes the problem of someone who does not yet know it exists.”",id:"note-12-handover",d:"4 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-04",img:"/media/notes/en/12-handover.jpg?v=e4329e0a5f"},{q:"“‘Reported’ and ‘resolved’ are not the same thing.”",id:"note-13-reported",d:"4 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-04",img:"/media/notes/en/13-reported.jpg?v=688bd4d02a"},{q:"“A team that is afraid to show its mistakes does not have fewer mistakes.”",id:"note-14-fear",d:"4 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-04",img:"/media/notes/en/14-fear.jpg?v=19b7e13a63"},{q:"“If the result depends on the right person being on shift, the organisation has knowledge, but it does not yet have a standard.”",id:"note-15-standard",d:"4 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-04",img:"/media/notes/en/15-standard.jpg?v=9fad8c8689"},{q:"“Reports tell me where to look. The floor tells me what is happening. A manager needs both.”",id:"note-16-reports",d:"4 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-04",img:"/media/notes/en/16-reports.jpg?v=fb7308ba99"},{q:"“A title can disappear in a single day. What you have learned does not.”",id:"note-17-the-title",d:"5 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-05",img:"/media/notes/en/17-the-title.jpg?v=44bff32f9c"},{q:"“The table is the starting point, not the answer.”",id:"note-18-the-table",d:"5 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-05",img:"/media/notes/en/18-the-table.jpg?v=812ecef2f3"},{q:"“A person has to know the standard before you judge them for not following it.”",id:"note-19-know-the-standard",d:"5 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-05",img:"/media/notes/en/19-know-the-standard.jpg?v=75c92c3aac"},{q:"“Pressure can be fair. Humiliating people is not a management method.”",id:"note-20-pressure",d:"5 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-05",img:"/media/notes/en/20-pressure.jpg?v=8ad1ed11a3"},{q:"“If the same mistake can happen with the next person, you have not changed the system. You have only changed the name in the report.”",id:"note-21-the-name",d:"5 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-05",img:"/media/notes/en/21-the-name.jpg?v=e5a623129d"},{q:"“Pressure must not be passed down as panic.”",id:"note-22-panic",d:"5 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-05",img:"/media/notes/en/22-panic.jpg?v=88b7c96b18"},{q:"“A KPI improves when you change the process that produces it.”",id:"note-23-the-process",d:"5 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-05",img:"/media/notes/en/23-the-process.jpg?v=f519f4f0cc"},{q:"“Accountability is not looking for someone to blame every time a number turns red. It is finding who owns the problem and following it until it is closed.”",id:"note-24-accountability",d:"5 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-05",img:"/media/notes/en/24-accountability.jpg?v=6cc2f9f154"},{q:"“The test of an SOP is not whether its author understands it. It is whether someone else can use it under pressure and get the same result.”",id:"note-25-the-test",d:"5 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-05",img:"/media/notes/en/25-the-test.jpg?v=9de4a28a01"},{q:"“When the official version says one thing and the people on shift have learned another, the SOP has stopped being a standard.”",id:"note-26-two-versions",d:"5 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-05",img:"/media/notes/en/26-two-versions.jpg?v=d68bdb3669"},{q:"“A problem only one person knows about is still a problem for the organisation. Once it is documented, it can have an owner.”",id:"note-27-written-down",d:"5 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-05",img:"/media/notes/en/27-written-down.jpg?v=da1e7aa269"},{q:"“Many mistakes are not born from a lack of skill. They are born from the sentence: ‘We'll do it later.’”",id:"note-28-later",d:"5 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-05",img:"/media/notes/en/28-later.jpg?v=21657e57a6"},{q:"“A mistake once can be chance. The same mistake several times is a process.”",id:"note-29-twice",d:"5 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-05",img:"/media/notes/en/29-twice.jpg?v=5f327fd03d"},{q:"“A handover is not just a transfer of information. It is a transfer of responsibility.”",id:"note-30-responsibility",d:"5 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-05",img:"/media/notes/en/30-responsibility.jpg?v=4a3a59bb26"},{q:"“If you keep covering the gaps in a system, you create the impression that the system works. Because someone is always rescuing it.”",id:"note-31-the-gaps",d:"5 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-05",img:"/media/notes/en/31-the-gaps.jpg?v=3ebc0f98c2"},{q:"“Standardisation is not meant to take thinking away from people. It is meant to stop them reinventing what the organisation should already know.”",id:"note-32-reinvent",d:"5 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-05",img:"/media/notes/en/32-reinvent.jpg?v=97b65cdf44"},{q:"“The data has to take me to the floor. And the floor has to help me understand the data.”",id:"note-33-the-floor",d:"5 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-05",img:"/media/notes/en/33-the-floor.jpg?v=34d0a311bc"},{q:"“In the first 30 days, a new manager does not need 30 solutions. They need 30 good questions.”",id:"note-34-thirty-questions",d:"5 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-05",img:"/media/notes/en/34-thirty-questions.jpg?v=930fe1674d"},{q:"“A step that looks unnecessary may be the step someone else depends on.”",id:"note-35-dependencies",d:"5 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-05",img:"/media/notes/en/35-dependencies.jpg?v=11365bdff5"},{q:"“The problem was not a lack of information. It was that the information did not quickly tell you where you were and what came next.”",id:"note-36-scattered",d:"5 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-05",img:"/media/notes/en/36-scattered.jpg?v=5740f2e9f7"},{q:"“The handover tells you what state you are inheriting. The briefing decides what matters now.”",id:"note-37-inherit-decide",d:"5 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-05",img:"/media/notes/en/37-inherit-decide.jpg?v=220ca93d47"},{q:"“If you only say the number and the shift starts, you have given information, not direction.”",id:"note-38-direction",d:"5 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-05",img:"/media/notes/en/38-direction.jpg?v=b6ff6213dd"},{q:"“A briefing makes sense when a KPI turns into a clear behaviour or action.”",id:"note-39-kpi-to-action",d:"5 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-05",img:"/media/notes/en/39-kpi-to-action.jpg?v=ceb5d321d7"},{q:"“If the training standard is ‘watch how I do it’, every new employee gets a different version of the same job.”",id:"note-40-versions",d:"8 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-08",img:"/media/notes/en/40-versions.jpg?v=947e7fdc83"},{q:"“‘Yes, I got it’ is not proof. Do it yourself. Tell me why. Show me what you do when an exception comes up.”",id:"note-41-proof",d:"8 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-08",img:"/media/notes/en/41-proof.jpg?v=da5804638c"},{q:"“Training is not measured by how well the trainer explained. It is measured by how consistent the result becomes once the trainer leaves.”",id:"note-42-trainer-leaves",d:"8 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-08",img:"/media/notes/en/42-trainer-leaves.jpg?v=bd8875c437"},{q:"“A good escalation system does not teach people to ask permission for everything. It teaches them to understand the limit of their own decision.”",id:"note-43-decision-limit",d:"8 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-08",img:"/media/notes/en/43-decision-limit.jpg?v=0b0840862b"},{q:"“Escalate the decision, not the ambiguity you could have cleared up yourself.”",id:"note-44-escalate-the-decision",d:"8 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-08",img:"/media/notes/en/44-escalate-the-decision.jpg?v=bd67618b05"},{q:"“Ownership does not mean solving it yourself. It means taking the problem to where the right decision can be made, with the right information.”",id:"note-45-ownership",d:"8 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-08",img:"/media/notes/en/45-ownership.jpg?v=709c37052b"},{q:"“The place where a mistake is measured is not necessarily the place where it was born.”",id:"note-46-measured-born",d:"8 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-08",img:"/media/notes/en/46-measured-born.jpg?v=985ee63ee5"},{q:"“Information sent is not always information received. And a problem reported is not necessarily a problem solved.”",id:"note-47-sent-received",d:"8 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-08",img:"/media/notes/en/47-sent-received.jpg?v=3a051658be"},{q:"“A process does not end when I hand the work over. It ends when the next team can carry it on without losing anything.”",id:"note-48-process-ends",d:"8 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-08",img:"/media/notes/en/48-process-ends.jpg?v=7fdd5d091b"},{q:"“A KPI can be mathematically correct and its interpretation still be unfair.”",id:"note-49-correct-unfair",d:"8 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-08",img:"/media/notes/en/49-correct-unfair.jpg?v=d24e5132ef"},{q:"“The manager's job is to separate what the person controls from what has to be corrected in the system.”",id:"note-50-person-system",d:"8 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-08",img:"/media/notes/en/50-person-system.jpg?v=ecc3ad37bf"},{q:"“One number shows the result. The other shows the reason. Without the second, numbers turn into reporting without learning.”",id:"note-51-result-reason",d:"8 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-08",img:"/media/notes/en/51-result-reason.jpg?v=ffbdb9d330"},{q:"“Pressure can be fair. Humiliation is not.”",id:"note-52-pressure",d:"8 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-08",img:"/media/notes/en/52-pressure.jpg?v=0b8b606cde"},{q:"“Formal authority gives you the right to make decisions. Trust is built by the way you make them.”",id:"note-53-authority-trust",d:"8 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-08",img:"/media/notes/en/53-authority-trust.jpg?v=3028c836f2"},{q:"“A mistake should lead to two questions: what did not work in the process, and what responsibility did the person have?”",id:"note-54-two-questions",d:"8 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-08",img:"/media/notes/en/54-two-questions.jpg?v=7f5df4f5c4"},{q:"“Not yet speaking a language well does not mean you are not good at your job.”",id:"note-55-language-ability",d:"8 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-08",img:"/media/notes/en/55-language-ability.jpg?v=2cb066d759"},{q:"“‘Did you understand?’ is not always enough. ‘Show me how you would do it’ is.”",id:"note-56-show-me",d:"8 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-08",img:"/media/notes/en/56-show-me.jpg?v=b9b5462033"},{q:"“A good standard is measured by how accurately different people can carry it out, even when they do not speak the same language.”",id:"note-57-standard-measured",d:"8 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-08",img:"/media/notes/en/57-standard-measured.jpg?v=00525e34a2"},{q:"“Search for the procedure, not the document.”",id:"note-58-search-procedure",d:"8 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-08",img:"/media/notes/en/58-search-procedure.jpg?v=de77849426"},{q:"“You can show the method of organising information without publishing the sensitive information the work relies on.”",id:"note-59-method-not-data",d:"8 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-08",img:"/media/notes/en/59-method-not-data.jpg?v=1e768596e2"},{q:"“An SOP becomes useful when the person who needs it can find it, understand it and apply it at the right moment.”",id:"note-60-sop-useful",d:"8 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-08",img:"/media/notes/en/60-sop-useful.jpg?v=b93abf378b"},{q:"“A partner is not managed like an employee. They need a reason to keep working with you.”",id:"note-61-partner",d:"8 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-08",img:"/media/notes/en/61-partner.jpg?v=31540141b1"},{q:"“Authority can help you make a decision. Trust is what keeps the cooperation going.”",id:"note-62-authority-trust",d:"8 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-08",img:"/media/notes/en/62-authority-trust.jpg?v=9d8d5c65a7"},{q:"“The goal is not a team that cannot work without me. It is a way of working that keeps running when I am not there.”",id:"note-63-runs-without-me",d:"8 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-08",img:"/media/notes/en/63-runs-without-me.jpg?v=97d25aa6b5"},{q:"“The document tells you how the work should be. The people tell you how it is.”",id:"note-64-document-people",d:"8 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-08",img:"/media/notes/en/64-document-people.jpg?v=da9ff187e9"},{q:"“Walk in to understand, not to show how much you know.”",id:"note-65-walk-in",d:"8 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-08",img:"/media/notes/en/65-walk-in.jpg?v=a92eaca705"},{q:"“Do not change something just because you want to show you have come to bring change.”",id:"note-66-change-to-show",d:"8 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-08",img:"/media/notes/en/66-change-to-show.jpg?v=b8b1045810"},{q:"“A new person's first days are a source of information most organisations waste.”",id:"note-67-new-eyes",d:"8 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-08",img:"/media/notes/en/67-new-eyes.jpg?v=0f8b35553c"},{q:"“A task without an owner is very close to a task nobody will do.”",id:"note-68-no-owner",d:"8 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-08",img:"/media/notes/en/68-no-owner.jpg?v=2863ded75d"},{q:"“A good briefing is not measured by how much was said. It is measured by what the team does differently in the first hour of the shift.”",id:"note-69-first-hour",d:"8 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-08",img:"/media/notes/en/69-first-hour.jpg?v=4bd8102bdb"},{q:"“Information gives you the pieces. A system gives you the order, the reason and the point where you know you can carry on alone.”",id:"note-70-pieces-order",d:"8 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-08",img:"/media/notes/en/70-pieces-order.jpg?v=e0b78d61ea"},{q:"“Without an SOP that is actually used, training becomes copying.”",id:"note-71-copying",d:"8 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-08",img:"/media/notes/en/71-copying.jpg?v=a45b60f9ba"},{q:"“Initiative makes sense within the limit you know. Beyond it, improvising is not courage. It is risk.”",id:"note-72-improvising",d:"8 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-08",img:"/media/notes/en/72-improvising.jpg?v=52aaced019"},{q:"“An operation that depends on who was on shift is not yet an operation that runs without you.”",id:"note-73-who-was-on-shift",d:"8 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-08",img:"/media/notes/en/73-who-was-on-shift.jpg?v=83a759d184"},{q:"“A complete escalation that comes late is worse than a short one that comes in time.”",id:"note-74-late-escalation",d:"8 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-08",img:"/media/notes/en/74-late-escalation.jpg?v=b3493172ba"},{q:"“A department can do its own work very well, and the operation can still fail.”",id:"note-75-between-departments",d:"8 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-08",img:"/media/notes/en/75-between-departments.jpg?v=0dee7b9f9f"},{q:"“The number tells you where to look for the problem, not who caused it.”",id:"note-76-where-not-who",d:"8 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-08",img:"/media/notes/en/76-where-not-who.jpg?v=3d4248ef80"},{q:"“A KPI the team trusts is not the one that always shows green. It is the one that measures clearly and is read fairly.”",id:"note-77-not-always-green",d:"8 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-08",img:"/media/notes/en/77-not-always-green.jpg?v=f7bad6aa10"},{q:"“If you start the conversation with the responsibility, you have judged before you listened.”",id:"note-78-judged-before-listening",d:"8 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-08",img:"/media/notes/en/78-judged-before-listening.jpg?v=ae4dc93b85"},{q:"“An unclear standard stays unclear in whatever language you translate it into.”",id:"note-79-unclear-any-language",d:"8 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-08",img:"/media/notes/en/79-unclear-any-language.jpg?v=2bba34d6d3"},{q:"“When someone does not understand an instruction, our job does not end with repeating the same sentence louder.”",id:"note-80-louder",d:"8 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-08",img:"/media/notes/en/80-louder.jpg?v=0b9e09b42e"},{q:"“The fact that I understand an instruction does not mean someone seeing it for the first time will understand it the same way.”",id:"note-81-first-time-reader",d:"8 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-08",img:"/media/notes/en/81-first-time-reader.jpg?v=622360b217"},{q:"“It is better to explain a limitation in time than to create an expectation you cannot meet.”",id:"note-82-explain-a-limit",d:"8 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-08",img:"/media/notes/en/82-explain-a-limit.jpg?v=fcc9aba65f"},{q:"“A manager's value is not how many things pass through their hands, but how well things keep going when they no longer do.”",id:"note-83-through-his-hands",d:"8 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-08",img:"/media/notes/en/83-through-his-hands.jpg?v=520dbd3da5"},{q:"“How do we solve it, why did it happen, and what do we change so it does not come back?”",id:"note-84-why-did-it-happen",d:"10 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-10",img:"/media/notes/en/84-why-did-it-happen.jpg?v=6866239c5a"},{q:"“The ten minutes before a shift are not for telling everything we know. They are for deciding what the team needs to know before the work starts.”",id:"note-85-ten-minutes",d:"10 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-10",img:"/media/notes/en/85-ten-minutes.jpg?v=b06ae01aea"},{q:"“Have I built an operation that works as a system, or an operation that depends on my presence?”",id:"note-86-system-or-presence",d:"10 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-10",img:"/media/notes/en/86-system-or-presence.jpg?v=3318cf2d2b"},{q:"“At which point did the work change hands, and what information was lost in that handover?”",id:"note-87-changed-hands",d:"10 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-10",img:"/media/notes/en/87-changed-hands.jpg?v=0cf0fbf328"},{q:"“Watch. Do it with me. You do it while I watch. Do it alone. Then explain it to me.”",id:"note-88-watch-do-explain",d:"10 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-10",img:"/media/notes/en/88-watch-do-explain.jpg?v=1166344eec"},{q:"“I will not ignore it because ‘it's not mine’.”",id:"note-89-not-mine",d:"10 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-10",img:"/media/notes/en/89-not-mine.jpg?v=333c1a66ee"},{q:"“Good management means seeing both, without looking for someone to blame at any cost and without hiding responsibility when it exists.”",id:"note-90-see-both",d:"10 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-10",img:"/media/notes/en/90-see-both.jpg?v=a6fc3e8087"},{q:"“A KPI tells you that you have a problem. It does not automatically tell you where it started or who caused it.”",id:"note-91-kpi-tells-problem",d:"10 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-10",img:"/media/notes/en/91-kpi-tells-problem.jpg?v=ac50a33807"},{q:"“Managing damage should not only be an effort to lower the percentage in the report. It should be an effort to understand and prevent damage in the process.”",id:"note-92-managing-damage-should",d:"10 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-10",img:"/media/notes/en/92-managing-damage-should.jpg?v=c2e5dfc921"},{q:"“The goal is not a lower percentage in the report. It is one less damaged unit in the process.”",id:"note-93-goal-lower-percentage",d:"10 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-10",img:"/media/notes/en/93-goal-lower-percentage.jpg?v=b46c6b3503"},{q:"“An order can reach the customer incomplete, but the problem may have started long before the delivery.”",id:"note-94-order-reach-customer",d:"10 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-10",img:"/media/notes/en/94-order-reach-customer.jpg?v=2fc98871ca"},{q:"“Incomplete should not be seen only as a negative number or a driver's mistake. It should help us understand where the product or the information went missing, and how we can stop it happening again.”",id:"note-95-incomplete-should-seen",d:"10 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-10",img:"/media/notes/en/95-incomplete-should-seen.jpg?v=d061a00773"},{q:"“The best check is not the one that counts incomplete orders. It is the one that stops them before they leave.”",id:"note-96-best-check-one",d:"10 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-10",img:"/media/notes/en/96-best-check-one.jpg?v=f1dda0aa6e"},{q:"“Gemba should not be an inspection walk. It should be a way to understand the process, to listen to people and to find the obstacles the numbers do not explain.”",id:"note-97-gemba-should-inspection",d:"10 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-10",img:"/media/notes/en/97-gemba-should-inspection.jpg?v=cb1043a78b"},{q:"“A manager who only sees the report knows the result of the work. A manager who also goes to the floor has a chance to understand how that result is made.”",id:"note-98-manager-who-only",d:"10 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-10",img:"/media/notes/en/98-manager-who-only.jpg?v=934bc71ba3"},{q:"“An organised ramp is not just cleaner. It makes loading clearer, lets mistakes be spotted sooner and lets people work in safer conditions.”",id:"note-99-organised-ramp-cleaner",d:"10 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-10",img:"/media/notes/en/99-organised-ramp-cleaner.jpg?v=f81f5a0974"},{q:"“Order is not proved by a poster on the wall. It is proved by how the workplace runs when the day is hard.”",id:"note-100-order-proved-by",d:"10 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-10",img:"/media/notes/en/100-order-proved-by.jpg?v=e57ddf6c09"},{q:"“6S should not be something done before an inspection. It should be part of the everyday way of working.”",id:"note-101-6s-should-something",d:"10 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-10",img:"/media/notes/en/101-6s-should-something.jpg?v=5f1f84d919"},{q:"“If we change the rules after every fluctuation, we risk creating more instability than improvement.”",id:"note-102-if-change-rules",d:"10 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-10",img:"/media/notes/en/102-if-change-rules.jpg?v=a9db6299ff"},{q:"“A manager has to know when to step in straight away and when to gather more information.”",id:"note-103-manager-know-when",d:"10 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-10",img:"/media/notes/en/103-manager-know-when.jpg?v=7a80c66d69"},{q:"“The KPI shows what happened. The trend helps us understand whether something is changing. The analysis of the process helps us decide what to do.”",id:"note-104-kpi-shows-happened",d:"10 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-10",img:"/media/notes/en/104-kpi-shows-happened.jpg?v=86f991c9b9"},{q:"“A bad day is a signal to check. It is not automatically proof that the whole process has to change.”",id:"note-105-bad-day-signal",d:"10 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-10",img:"/media/notes/en/105-bad-day-signal.jpg?v=7ff224f36a"},{q:"“The value of DMAIC lies in the discipline not to jump straight from the problem to the solution.”",id:"note-106-value-dmaic-lies",d:"10 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-10",img:"/media/notes/en/106-value-dmaic-lies.jpg?v=3369ce7c65"},{q:"“A problem is not solved just because it did not happen again today.”",id:"note-107-problem-solved-happen",d:"10 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-10",img:"/media/notes/en/107-problem-solved-happen.jpg?v=742f931c07"},{q:"“When you cannot see the vehicle, you need a reliable way to understand what is happening with it.”",id:"note-108-when-cannot-see",d:"10 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-10",img:"/media/notes/en/108-when-cannot-see.jpg?v=70923cf0f8"},{q:"“Remote coordination is not just giving drivers instructions. It is building a way of communicating in which problems become visible, responsibilities are clear and decisions are taken in time.”",id:"note-109-remote-coordination-giving",d:"10 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-10",img:"/media/notes/en/109-remote-coordination-giving.jpg?v=2eb4a90a6a"},{q:"“Pressure does not always create the problems. Often it makes them more visible.”",id:"note-110-pressure-always-create",d:"10 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-10",img:"/media/notes/en/110-pressure-always-create.jpg?v=2956033548"},{q:"“Capacity is not just the number of people you have available. It is the number of people who can do the work to the standard.”",id:"note-111-capacity-number-people",d:"10 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-10",img:"/media/notes/en/111-capacity-number-people.jpg?v=af3301571c"},{q:"“The standard is not proved on the day everything goes to plan. It is proved on the day the plan is not enough.”",id:"note-112-standard-proved-day",d:"10 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-10",img:"/media/notes/en/112-standard-proved-day.jpg?v=9c6b775763"},{q:"“At night, the options for a solution are not always the same as during the day. But that does not mean the responsibility for the problem should get lost.”",id:"note-113-night-options-solution",d:"10 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-10",img:"/media/notes/en/113-night-options-solution.jpg?v=29a2253e95"},{q:"“A complaint is not closed just because the guest walks away from the front desk.”",id:"note-114-complaint-closed-guest",d:"10 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-10",img:"/media/notes/en/114-complaint-closed-guest.jpg?v=7f9689178c"},{q:"“Professionalism is listening, checking, doing what is within your remit and making sure the work carries on when someone else has to be involved.”",id:"note-115-professionalism-listening-checking",d:"10 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-10",img:"/media/notes/en/115-professionalism-listening-checking.jpg?v=b740062202"},{q:"“The guest should not pay in time and nerves for the fact that the hotel works in shifts.”",id:"note-116-guest-should-pay",d:"10 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-10",img:"/media/notes/en/116-guest-should-pay.jpg?v=ebc771ef7c"},{q:"“A standard that exists only in a document is not necessarily a standard that is applied.”",id:"note-117-standard-exists-only",d:"10 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-10",img:"/media/notes/en/117-standard-exists-only.jpg?v=c72ee77e20"},{q:"“Have we built an improvement that becomes part of the system, or a temporary result that depends on the manager's attention?”",id:"note-118-built-improvement-becomes",d:"10 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-10",img:"/media/notes/en/118-built-improvement-becomes.jpg?v=96234ebdc7"},{q:"“Real improvement is not the kind that only works while the manager is there. It is the kind that keeps working when the manager leaves.”",id:"note-119-real-improvement-kind",d:"10 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-10",img:"/media/notes/en/119-real-improvement-kind.jpg?v=accb575de0"},{q:"“A good manager can improve a working day. A good system keeps the improvement alive even on the day the manager is not there.”",id:"note-120-good-manager-improve",d:"10 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-10",img:"/media/notes/en/120-good-manager-improve.jpg?v=965460f70a"},{q:"“The industry changes. The thing you control changes. But the management problem stays the same: if information, responsibility and execution do not meet at the same point, a mistake will show up somewhere.”",id:"note-121-industry-changes-problem",d:"12 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-12",img:"/media/notes/en/121-industry-changes-problem.jpg?v=7558f1371a"},{q:"“The customer does not much care which department made the mistake. They only see the company in front of them.”",id:"note-122-customer-sees-company",d:"12 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-12",img:"/media/notes/en/122-customer-sees-company.jpg?v=2f37cb3211"},{q:"“Management is not always having authority over someone. Often it is getting people you have no authority over to work in the same direction as you.”",id:"note-123-without-authority-direction",d:"12 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-12",img:"/media/notes/en/123-without-authority-direction.jpg?v=47822453fb"},{q:"“You can learn the industry. What is harder to learn is to see when a process is not working, not to walk past the problem, and to take it on and see it through.”",id:"note-124-learn-the-industry",d:"12 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-12",img:"/media/notes/en/124-learn-the-industry.jpg?v=912616b411"},{q:"“Do not walk into the new job expecting others to respect what you used to be. Start showing what you can do where you are.”",id:"note-125-show-what-you-can",d:"12 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-12",img:"/media/notes/en/125-show-what-you-can.jpg?v=baaa002168"},{q:"“If I had thought some jobs were beneath me, I might never have learned what I needed to rise again.”",id:"note-126-jobs-beneath-me",d:"12 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-12",img:"/media/notes/en/126-jobs-beneath-me.jpg?v=1521f2b785"},{q:"“The floor is not only a place to look. It is a place to reconstruct what happened.”",id:"note-127-floor-reconstruct",d:"12 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-12",img:"/media/notes/en/127-floor-reconstruct.jpg?v=5560dfac1e"},{q:"“What you see has to be written down, otherwise tomorrow it is only a memory.”",id:"note-128-written-down-memory",d:"12 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-12",img:"/media/notes/en/128-written-down-memory.jpg?v=136557c8af"},{q:"“Respect is not never holding someone accountable. Respect is making the standard clear to them, listening to them before you judge them, and, when the responsibility is theirs, not hiding that from them.”",id:"note-129-respect-accountable",d:"12 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-12",img:"/media/notes/en/129-respect-accountable.jpg?v=907c49f726"},{q:"“A standard can be very strong without treating a person as a number.”",id:"note-130-standard-strong-number",d:"12 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-12",img:"/media/notes/en/130-standard-strong-number.jpg?v=07af2598ed"},{q:"“Pareto does not give you the truth if the data you feed it does not describe the truth.”",id:"note-131-pareto-truth",d:"12 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-12",img:"/media/notes/en/131-pareto-truth.jpg?v=a1ba43cf37"},{q:"“When the only answer an analysis gives is ‘the employee was careless’, very often the analysis has ended too early.”",id:"note-132-analysis-ended-early",d:"12 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-12",img:"/media/notes/en/132-analysis-ended-early.jpg?v=d8fffe6605"},{q:"“If a process only works because a good person remembers it, you do not yet have a good process.”",id:"note-133-good-person-remembers",d:"12 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-12",img:"/media/notes/en/133-good-person-remembers.jpg?v=6cd1cae25a"},{q:"“Process matters, but people are not processes. An employee can have the same task as yesterday and come to work today in a completely different state.”",id:"note-134-people-not-processes",d:"12 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-12",img:"/media/notes/en/134-people-not-processes.jpg?v=bdbb457a97"},{q:"“If a process worked because I knew it, today I would try to make the system know it.”",id:"note-135-system-know-it",d:"12 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-12",img:"/media/notes/en/135-system-know-it.jpg?v=e41bca3e03"},{q:"“A message that needs three follow-up questions to be understood has lost the time it was supposed to save.”",id:"note-136-message-follow-up",d:"12 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-12",img:"/media/notes/en/136-message-follow-up.jpg?v=cdd903747a"},{q:"“One delay is an event. The same delay, in the same place, several days in a row, is a pattern.”",id:"note-137-delay-pattern",d:"12 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-12",img:"/media/notes/en/137-delay-pattern.jpg?v=492ef9f351"},{q:"“On the ramp, the problem appears in front of you. From a distance, either you go looking for it, or you have built a way for it to come to you.”",id:"note-138-come-to-you",d:"12 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-12",img:"/media/notes/en/138-come-to-you.jpg?v=b96f8dfc4c"},{q:"“You do not need a Black Belt certificate to ask good questions. But knowing the name of a method is not enough to claim you have applied it.”",id:"note-139-name-of-method",d:"12 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-12",img:"/media/notes/en/139-name-of-method.jpg?v=21c049ddc8"},{q:"“If an improvement only holds as long as one person is there, it was not an improvement of the process. It was one person's presence.”",id:"note-140-one-persons-presence",d:"12 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-12",img:"/media/notes/en/140-one-persons-presence.jpg?v=4d9c7e58a0"},{q:"“A process that is being inspected behaves differently while the manager is there.”",id:"note-141-inspected-behaves",d:"12 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-12",img:"/media/notes/en/141-inspected-behaves.jpg?v=6aa6e1db93"},{q:"“Someone sees the problem, asks about it, and the question goes unanswered. The next day the problem is still there, but now it looks normal.”",id:"note-142-looks-normal",d:"12 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-12",img:"/media/notes/en/142-looks-normal.jpg?v=f30d20f105"},{q:"“An SOP that is only read can look very professional. But when the pressure of the shift begins, nobody has time to read a manual.”",id:"note-143-manual-pressure",d:"12 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-12",img:"/media/notes/en/143-manual-pressure.jpg?v=98d9f2ff6a"},{q:"“A document tells you how the work should be done. A good SOP helps you do the work correctly at exactly the moment you need it.”",id:"note-144-sop-right-moment",d:"12 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-12",img:"/media/notes/en/144-sop-right-moment.jpg?v=711cdefc4f"},{q:"“A night shift does not end when the system closes. It ends when the person who comes after me clearly understands what happened, what was solved and what is left to follow up.”",id:"note-145-night-shift-ends",d:"12 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-12",img:"/media/notes/en/145-night-shift-ends.jpg?v=dae33e6fbc"},{q:"“Responsibility is not making every decision. Responsibility is knowing which decision you can make yourself and which one you should not make.”",id:"note-146-which-decision",d:"12 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-12",img:"/media/notes/en/146-which-decision.jpg?v=380a7cfa09"},{q:"“A good report should not only describe the past. It should make the day that is starting safer.”",id:"note-147-report-safer",d:"12 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-12",img:"/media/notes/en/147-report-safer.jpg?v=45b4eade25"},{q:"“I did not want to remember where every document was. I wanted to know where to go for the right answer.”",id:"note-148-where-to-go",d:"12 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-12",img:"/media/notes/en/148-where-to-go.jpg?v=b55ef6d702"},{q:"“A manager can be demanding, decisive and very clear without violating the dignity of the person in front of them.”",id:"note-149-demanding-dignity",d:"12 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-12",img:"/media/notes/en/149-demanding-dignity.jpg?v=9f153c377c"},{q:"“The point of the conversation after a mistake is not that the employee leaves afraid of the next one. It is that they leave knowing what to do differently.”",id:"note-150-leave-knowing",d:"12 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-12",img:"/media/notes/en/150-leave-knowing.jpg?v=4878bafe7d"},{q:"“When everything has its place, the thing that is out of place catches the eye. When nothing has a fixed place, nothing looks out of place.”",id:"note-151-out-of-place",d:"12 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-12",img:"/media/notes/en/151-out-of-place.jpg?v=a679fd9f54"},{q:"“Safety is not the last S added to the list. It is the reason the list exists.”",id:"note-152-reason-list-exists",d:"12 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-12",img:"/media/notes/en/152-reason-list-exists.jpg?v=208f86e68a"},{q:"“A tidy area with an open problem nobody knows about is not a tidy area.”",id:"note-153-tidy-area",d:"12 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-12",img:"/media/notes/en/153-tidy-area.jpg?v=0836fecedd"},{q:"“A plan that only works when everything goes as forecast is not a plan for the hard day. It is a description of an ordinary one.”",id:"note-154-ordinary-day-plan",d:"12 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-12",img:"/media/notes/en/154-ordinary-day-plan.jpg?v=6dad331dc4"},{q:"“On the hard day, something will be pushed back. The question is whether you decided beforehand what is never pushed back, or whether you decide it in the middle of the pressure.”",id:"note-155-never-pushed-back",d:"12 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-12",img:"/media/notes/en/155-never-pushed-back.jpg?v=b85d89b8ce"},{q:"“A standard that can only be followed when there is spare time is not a standard. It is a wish.”",id:"note-156-standard-wish",d:"12 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-12",img:"/media/notes/en/156-standard-wish.jpg?v=3eabe47f0c"},{q:"“An improvement that depends on the manager's attention lasts as long as the attention does.”",id:"note-157-attention-lasts",d:"12 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-12",img:"/media/notes/en/157-attention-lasts.jpg?v=91a7a9ac5b"},{q:"“The percentage tells you how much. The questions tell you where. And change begins with the ‘where’.”",id:"note-158-only-where-changed",d:"12 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-12",img:"/media/notes/en/158-only-where-changed.jpg?v=18f4809258"},{q:"“At the customer's door, a missing bag is a complaint. At the ramp, it is still a question.”",id:"note-159-still-a-question",d:"12 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-12",img:"/media/notes/en/159-still-a-question.jpg?v=658616ab30"},{q:"“A standard does not only say what is done. It also says where.”",id:"note-160-also-says-where",d:"12 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-12",img:"/media/notes/en/160-also-says-where.jpg?v=cf28ce18c7"},{q:"“The system is faster than you in everything it was told. It knows nothing of what it was not told. And most of what the floor knows has never been told to anyone.”",id:"note-161-system-faster-than",d:"13 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-13",img:"/media/notes/en/161-system-faster-than.jpg?v=f78a66d278"},{q:"“The system decides first. What is left for you is the part it was never told, and the name that answers for all of it.”",id:"note-162-system-decides-first",d:"13 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-13",img:"/media/notes/en/162-system-decides-first.jpg?v=c68ec9e0cd"},{q:"“Do not confuse losing the title with losing your professional value.”",id:"note-163-confuse-losing-title",d:"13 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-13",img:"/media/notes/en/163-confuse-losing-title.jpg?v=d93046f47f"},{q:"“A rule like that looks small on paper. On the ramp it is the difference between a problem caught in time and a customer who receives an incomplete order.”",id:"note-164-rule-like-looks",d:"13 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-13",img:"/media/notes/en/164-rule-like-looks.jpg?v=5021469983"},{q:"“The standard was not a poster on the wall. It came with expectations, checks and accountability.”",id:"note-165-standard-was-poster",d:"13 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-13",img:"/media/notes/en/165-standard-was-poster.jpg?v=97739136c3"},{q:"“The wrong category leads you, with great confidence, to the wrong cause.”",id:"note-166-wrong-category-leads",d:"13 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-13",img:"/media/notes/en/166-wrong-category-leads.jpg?v=cd4bd42871"},{q:"“Taking on more responsibility does not mean making decisions that are not yours to make.”",id:"note-167-taking-more-responsibility",d:"13 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-13",img:"/media/notes/en/167-taking-more-responsibility.jpg?v=5be303d19e"},{q:"“Job titles change faster than human nature. Pressure, misunderstanding, responsibility and the need to communicate exist everywhere.”",id:"note-168-job-titles-change",d:"13 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-13",img:"/media/notes/en/168-job-titles-change.jpg?v=fd57a73185"},{q:"“I take particular care that an open problem does not look like a finished one just because my shift is ending.”",id:"note-169-care-especially-unclosed",d:"13 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-13",img:"/media/notes/en/169-care-especially-unclosed.jpg?v=da85a50063"},{q:"“While building it I understood that the most important challenge was not making a nice page. It was organising the information so that it could be used, checked and improved.”",id:"note-170-building-understood-most",d:"13 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-13",img:"/media/notes/en/170-building-understood-most.jpg?v=0a6ca28f92"},{q:"“If the team understands a KPI one way and the report calculates it another, trust is lost before the first result is even seen.”",id:"note-171-if-team-understands",d:"13 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-13",img:"/media/notes/en/171-if-team-understands.jpg?v=ff50e97712"},{q:"“The question is not whether today is worse than the average. Many days will be. The question is whether today is worse than the normal variation of this process.”",id:"note-172-question-whether-today",d:"13 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-13",img:"/media/notes/en/172-question-whether-today.jpg?v=f48bde0226"},{q:"“In operations, the temptation is always to jump to the solution. The KPI comes out bad, and someone has a solution straight away.”",id:"note-173-operations-temptation-always",d:"13 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-13",img:"/media/notes/en/173-operations-temptation-always.jpg?v=cdc369bbda"},{q:"“You are so far inside the work that you may stop seeing the process as a process.”",id:"note-174-far-inside-work",d:"13 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-13",img:"/media/notes/en/174-far-inside-work.jpg?v=b51e94fdf7"},{q:"“A promise that does not depend on you does not solve the problem. It pushes it to the morning, and makes it heavier.”",id:"note-175-promise-depend-solve",d:"13 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-13",img:"/media/notes/en/175-promise-depend-solve.jpg?v=93469d878b"},{q:"“The driver sees the problem. The dispatcher sees its effect on the whole shift. The manager has to understand why the problem exists.”",id:"note-176-driver-sees-problem",d:"13 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-13",img:"/media/notes/en/176-driver-sees-problem.jpg?v=418488b76e"},{q:"“An SOP cannot be treated as a document that is written once and then forgotten.”",id:"note-177-sop-cannot-treated",d:"13 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-13",img:"/media/notes/en/177-sop-cannot-treated.jpg?v=d560689bc8"},{q:"“It is not always good for a leader to become the person who solves everything.”",id:"note-178-always-good-leader",d:"13 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-13",img:"/media/notes/en/178-always-good-leader.jpg?v=28d3f0c3b2"},{q:"“A briefing loses its value when it stays with the numbers.”",id:"note-179-briefing-loses-value",d:"13 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-13",img:"/media/notes/en/179-briefing-loses-value.jpg?v=f19f845fb6"},{q:"“Inside a team it is usually clear who does what. There is someone responsible, a standard, a rhythm. But work rarely stays inside a single team.”",id:"note-180-inside-team-usually",d:"13 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-13",img:"/media/notes/en/180-inside-team-usually.jpg?v=435d4091a6"},{q:"“If we look only at the person, we risk leaving untouched a process that will produce the same problem again.”",id:"note-181-if-look-only",d:"13 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-13",img:"/media/notes/en/181-if-look-only.jpg?v=021f6bd4db"},{q:"“A manager has to tell a lack of professional ability apart from a communication barrier. They are two different problems and they need different solutions.”",id:"note-182-manager-tell-lack",d:"13 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-13",img:"/media/notes/en/182-manager-tell-lack.jpg?v=3c56486fde"},{q:"“When the process is not written down as a clear path, it lives in the person who does it every day.”",id:"note-183-when-process-written",d:"13 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-13",img:"/media/notes/en/183-when-process-written.jpg?v=dea55dcc86"},{q:"“When information arrives late, the lateness itself is a signal. The problem has had time to grow before you learn about it.”",id:"note-184-when-information-arrives",d:"13 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-13",img:"/media/notes/en/184-when-information-arrives.jpg?v=013f5ea8f7"},{q:"“On paper there was a reserve. In practice, the reserve was already taken.”",id:"note-185-paper-there-was",d:"13 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-13",img:"/media/notes/en/185-paper-there-was.jpg?v=1de28979dd"},{q:"“A good document is useful. But on its own it does not guarantee that the process is followed correctly.”",id:"note-186-good-document-useful",d:"13 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-13",img:"/media/notes/en/186-good-document-useful.jpg?v=badab066db"},{q:"“When a problem is solved in a hurry, the place is the first thing people forget.”",id:"note-187-when-problem-solved",d:"13 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-13",img:"/media/notes/en/187-when-problem-solved.jpg?v=cf981a517d"},{q:"“A correction that repeats is not a correction. It is a fault in the system that nobody has reported.”",id:"note-188-correction-repeats-correction",d:"13 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-13",img:"/media/notes/en/188-correction-repeats-correction.jpg?v=3401c83a28"},{q:"“A red number is not the floor. It is a report about the floor, and a report has an age.”",id:"note-189-red-number-report",d:"13 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-13",img:"/media/notes/en/189-red-number-report.jpg?v=c1180575e5"},{q:"“The red colour is a signal to check. It is not a diagnosis.”",id:"note-190-signal-not-diagnosis",d:"13 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-13",img:"/media/notes/en/190-signal-not-diagnosis.jpg?v=8cc0762974"},{q:"“A red number tells you where to look. It does not tell you what is there now. The distance between the two is the age of the number, and knowing it is your job.”",id:"note-191-where-to-look",d:"13 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-13",img:"/media/notes/en/191-where-to-look.jpg?v=d8a894abc3"},{q:"“The status in the system and the full history of a problem are not the same thing.”",id:"note-192-status-not-history",d:"13 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-13",img:"/media/notes/en/192-status-not-history.jpg?v=f39fbd4f73"},{q:"“The system plans the tour with the data it has. The driver drives it with the conditions they have. Neither has the whole of it without the other.”",id:"note-193-system-plans-tour",d:"13 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-13",img:"/media/notes/en/193-system-plans-tour.jpg?v=1a850c5bab"},{q:"“An experienced driver should not be the permanent correction of a system that does not learn.”",id:"note-194-experienced-driver-should",d:"13 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-13",img:"/media/notes/en/194-experienced-driver-should.jpg?v=f9207f434b"},{q:"“The problem is not only when the system does not know the tour. The problem is when the organisation does not learn from the people who drive it every day.”",id:"note-195-problem-system-know",d:"13 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-13",img:"/media/notes/en/195-problem-system-know.jpg?v=77b25484b6"},{q:"“The tour the driver does not understand is sometimes an error in the plan, sometimes something nobody has explained to them. You can only tell which it is when someone listens, verifies it and writes it down.”",id:"note-196-tour-driver-understand",d:"13 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-13",img:"/media/notes/en/196-tour-driver-understand.jpg?v=e8735b2c1a"},{q:"“An accurate record is not always proof that the physical process ended correctly.”",id:"note-197-accurate-record-always",d:"13 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-13",img:"/media/notes/en/197-accurate-record-always.jpg?v=630838c254"},{q:"“The scanner is a witness to an action. Judging requires understanding the whole process.”",id:"note-198-scanner-witness-action",d:"13 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-13",img:"/media/notes/en/198-scanner-witness-action.jpg?v=56a2ee0e44"},{q:"“The system tells you what has been recorded. The manager has to understand what has happened. Between the two is the process, and that is where the work is done.”",id:"note-199-system-tells-been",d:"13 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-13",img:"/media/notes/en/199-system-tells-been.jpg?v=0e754a2144"},{q:"“Two reports with two different numbers do not mean that one of them is wrong. They mean you have to know what each one counts.”",id:"note-200-two-reports-two",d:"13 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-13",img:"/media/notes/en/200-two-reports-two.jpg?v=7997f91ab6"},{q:"“Generating a report does not automatically mean that every operational issue has been closed.”",id:"note-201-generating-report-automatically",d:"13 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-13",img:"/media/notes/en/201-generating-report-automatically.jpg?v=1b0c71a07f"},{q:"“AI can help me write a report more clearly. It must not decide by itself what is true.”",id:"note-202-ai-help-me",d:"13 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-13",img:"/media/notes/en/202-ai-help-me.jpg?v=57f1ce36f9"},{q:"“A report should help a person understand reality, not replace the checking of reality.”",id:"note-203-report-should-help",d:"13 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-13",img:"/media/notes/en/203-report-should-help.jpg?v=cf85082720"},{q:"“The machine can write the report. The responsibility for what the report says has to stay with a person.”",id:"note-204-machine-write-report",d:"13 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-13",img:"/media/notes/en/204-machine-write-report.jpg?v=e804e92cad"},{q:"“When many processes depend on one system, its interruption affects not only the way people work, but also the way they learn.”",id:"note-205-many-processes-depend",d:"13 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-13",img:"/media/notes/en/205-many-processes-depend.jpg?v=db79801e2e"},{q:"“The system coming back is not the end of the incident.”",id:"note-206-system-coming-back",d:"13 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-13",img:"/media/notes/en/206-system-coming-back.jpg?v=77c96e3a43"},{q:"“A prepared operation is not one that pretends the system will never stop. It is one that knows how to keep responsibility and the continuity of the work when the system stops.”",id:"note-207-prepared-operation-pretends",d:"13 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-13",img:"/media/notes/en/207-prepared-operation-pretends.jpg?v=5e9f216dc1"},{q:"“When the system stops, you realise how much of your work depends on it, and how well prepared you are to carry on.”",id:"note-208-system-stops-realise",d:"13 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-13",img:"/media/notes/en/208-system-stops-realise.jpg?v=e41f1e5264"},{q:"“A new system does not become part of the work because it has been installed. It does when people understand it, know how to use it, and know what to do when it does not help them.”",id:"note-209-new-system-become",d:"13 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-13",img:"/media/notes/en/209-new-system-become.jpg?v=f3a0a5b60c"},{q:"“The difficulty of a new system is not only knowing where to click. It is finding the right information at the moment you need it.”",id:"note-210-difficulty-new-system",d:"13 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-13",img:"/media/notes/en/210-difficulty-new-system.jpg?v=ddeff78d7e"},{q:"“Installation changes the system. Training, communication and daily experience change the way people work.”",id:"note-211-installation-changes-system",d:"13 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-13",img:"/media/notes/en/211-installation-changes-system.jpg?v=4a7e4c5eec"},{q:"“When an employee builds a tool to make the work easier, they may be showing a gap in the way the organisation distributes information.”",id:"note-212-employee-builds-tool",d:"13 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-13",img:"/media/notes/en/212-employee-builds-tool.jpg?v=7bea9428e3"},{q:"“A useful tool becomes a team tool only when it is accurate, up to date, authorised for the use it is given, and safe for the information it handles.”",id:"note-213-useful-tool-becomes",d:"13 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-13",img:"/media/notes/en/213-useful-tool-becomes.jpg?v=d0f1b00aeb"},{q:"“A small tool can solve a big problem. But to become part of the work, it has to be more than the project of the person who built it.”",id:"note-214-small-tool-solve",d:"13 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-13",img:"/media/notes/en/214-small-tool-solve.jpg?v=5873d054da"},{q:"“Containment buys you time. It does not buy you the cause. An 8D that stops at containment has only moved the problem out of the customer's sight.”",id:"note-215-containment-buys-time",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/215-containment-buys-time.jpg?v=84faa0d1fa"},{q:"“Every defect a customer saw has two causes: why it was made, and why nobody caught it before it left. An 8D that fixes only the first leaves the escape point open.”",id:"note-216-every-defect-customer",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/216-every-defect-customer.jpg?v=f32667819f"},{q:"“A risk assessment written for the inspector protects the paper. One written with the people who do the work protects the people.”",id:"note-217-risk-assessment-written",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/217-risk-assessment-written.jpg?v=a3ed0d6b19"},{q:"“A warning sign is the last line of defence, not the first. Remove the hazard before you ask people to be careful around it.”",id:"note-218-warning-sign-last",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/218-warning-sign-last.jpg?v=e843d45676"},{q:"“A strategy that nobody on the floor can explain is not a strategy. It is a slide.”",id:"note-219-strategy-nobody-floor",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/219-strategy-nobody-floor.jpg?v=9d114fe046"},{q:"“Goals that only travel downwards return as excuses. Goals passed back and forth return as commitments. That is what catchball is for.”",id:"note-220-goals-only-travel",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/220-goals-only-travel.jpg?v=4967b6d93e"},{q:"“Most of a changeover is work that could have been done before the machine stopped.”",id:"note-221-most-changeover-work",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/221-most-changeover-work.jpg?v=1e73fbe852"},{q:"“Every minute you take out of a changeover is a minute the line gives back without a single extra person.”",id:"note-222-every-minute-take",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/222-every-minute-take.jpg?v=1a0d0b3c4e"},{q:"“Leader standard work exists for one reason: so that the team's standard survives the leader's busiest day.”",id:"note-223-leader-standard-work",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/223-leader-standard-work.jpg?v=6c70884e8b"},{q:"“Understaffing is rarely a surprise. It is usually a forecast that nobody turned into capacity.”",id:"note-224-understaffing-rarely-surprise",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/224-understaffing-rarely-surprise.jpg?v=23209b64fe"},{q:"“Overtime is not a capacity plan. It is the bill for not having one.”",id:"note-225-overtime-capacity-plan",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/225-overtime-capacity-plan.jpg?v=42ec1e1055"},{q:"“Count all stock with the same care and you count the stock that matters with too little.”",id:"note-226-count-all-stock",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/226-count-all-stock.jpg?v=3d9bff7671"},{q:"“Safety stock is not a feeling. It is the price of the demand you cannot predict.”",id:"note-227-safety-stock-feeling",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/227-safety-stock-feeling.jpg?v=30e5d41681"},{q:"“A guest waiting in the lobby is rarely a housekeeping problem. It is usually a room status that nobody updated.”",id:"note-228-guest-waiting-lobby",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/228-guest-waiting-lobby.jpg?v=c28a8fe99c"},{q:"“Give every attendant the same number of rooms as yesterday and you have planned nothing: a departure and a stay-over are not the same work.”",id:"note-229-give-every-attendant",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/229-give-every-attendant.jpg?v=14ec8c6cb1"},{q:"“Service recovery begins before the compensation. A guest who feels heard often asks for less than a guest who feels handled.”",id:"note-230-service-recovery-begins",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/230-service-recovery-begins.jpg?v=282041c6e3"},{q:"“A guest's complaint is not closed when the guest leaves the desk. It is closed when you call back and the answer is yes.”",id:"note-231-guests-complaint-closed",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/231-guests-complaint-closed.jpg?v=ae6b71e349"},{q:"“Preventive maintenance always looks expensive until you price the breakdown it stopped.”",id:"note-232-preventive-maintenance-always",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/232-preventive-maintenance-always.jpg?v=61b0515dba"},{q:"“A postponed maintenance job is not saved time. It is a breakdown with a date you did not choose.”",id:"note-233-postponed-maintenance-job",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/233-postponed-maintenance-job.jpg?v=7b0c806d67"},{q:"“A good morning list does not tell you everything that happened. It tells you the three things that cannot wait.”",id:"note-234-good-morning-list",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/234-good-morning-list.jpg?v=dbb191e276"},{q:"“Comparing sites side by side is not about naming the worst one. It is about finding out what the best one does that the others do not.”",id:"note-235-comparing-sites-side",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/235-comparing-sites-side.jpg?v=a72f58da79"},{q:"“A board on the wall reaches people a screen never will. The team that never logs in still reads what is on paper.”",id:"note-236-board-wall-reaches",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/236-board-wall-reaches.jpg?v=24fded6525"},{q:"“An action without an owner and a date is a wish written down in a meeting.”",id:"note-237-action-without-owner",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/237-action-without-owner.jpg?v=482f5c6dc3"},{q:"“Layered audits work for one reason: when the site lead checks the same standard as the team lead, the standard stops being the team lead's problem alone.”",id:"note-238-layered-audits-work",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/238-layered-audits-work.jpg?v=18af553c51"},{q:"“If only one person can do the job, you do not have a process. You have a holiday you cannot approve.”",id:"note-239-if-only-one",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/239-if-only-one.jpg?v=bb01ea9815"},{q:"“A room released without inspection is inspected anyway: by the guest, at the worst moment.”",id:"note-240-room-released-without",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/240-room-released-without.jpg?v=2062b2ddcf"},{q:"“Nobody writes walking into the job description. Yet on many shifts, walking is the job.”",id:"note-241-nobody-writes-walking",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/241-nobody-writes-walking.jpg?v=41f175113b"},{q:"“A family business that pays its own children in promises is not building a future. It is spending it.”",id:"note-242-family-business-pays",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/242-family-business-pays.jpg?v=8f8db9daee"},{q:"“Blood can be a bond. Used to deny someone their pay, it becomes a chain.”",id:"note-243-blood-bond-used",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/243-blood-bond-used.jpg?v=285dd62a74"},{q:"“A surname can be inherited. Competence cannot.”",id:"note-244-surname-inherited-competence",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/244-surname-inherited-competence.jpg?v=2d9fdd3637"},{q:"“When the owner rewards the one who went over the manager's head, they do not save a person. They switch off the system.”",id:"note-245-when-owner-rewards",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/245-when-owner-rewards.jpg?v=c3dddd3d52"},{q:"“Going home when the shift ends is not a lack of loyalty. Unplanned overtime every day is a lack of management.”",id:"note-246-going-home-when",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/246-going-home-when.jpg?v=4edf29410b"},{q:"“When a good person leaves, it is not the market that failed. It is management.”",id:"note-247-when-good-person",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/247-when-good-person.jpg?v=b5824cd51e"},{q:"“A wage is not bread you are given. It is the price of the work you gave.”",id:"note-248-wage-bread-given",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/248-wage-bread-given.jpg?v=169e89fb05"},{q:"“Sweating every day over the same failure is not dedication. It is a process nobody fixed.”",id:"note-249-sweating-every-day",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/249-sweating-every-day.jpg?v=b862955b75"},{q:"“A pay rise that insults costs more than no rise at all: it tells people exactly what their year was worth to you.”",id:"note-250-pay-rise-insults",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/250-pay-rise-insults.jpg?v=67c5721ec8"},{q:"“When Human Resources forget the human, all that is left is the stamp.”",id:"note-251-when-human-resources",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/251-when-human-resources.jpg?v=ec6b054fa3"},{q:"“The noise of motion is not progress. A leader who needs to look busy has usually stopped looking at the work.”",id:"note-252-noise-motion-progress",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/252-noise-motion-progress.jpg?v=d55d63088d"},{q:"“A machine that runs all shift is not necessarily a machine that produces. OEE shows you the difference in minutes.”",id:"note-253-machine-runs-all",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/253-machine-runs-all.jpg?v=508b640a44"},{q:"“The biggest loss is rarely the breakdown everyone remembers. It is the small stops nobody writes down.”",id:"note-254-biggest-loss-rarely",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/254-biggest-loss-rarely.jpg?v=7bc55fa2c5"},{q:"“A fishbone filled in by one person is a guess with a diagram around it.”",id:"note-255-fishbone-filled-by",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/255-fishbone-filled-by.jpg?v=9b4086a4bc"},{q:"“An FMEA asks the uncomfortable question while the answer is still cheap: how can this step fail?”",id:"note-256-fmea-asks-uncomfortable",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/256-fmea-asks-uncomfortable.jpg?v=2e671753c2"},{q:"“You cannot balance a line on opinions about how long a job takes. A stopwatch is fairer than a feeling.”",id:"note-257-cannot-balance-line",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/257-cannot-balance-line.jpg?v=12341796cb"},{q:"“Takt is not a target to push people towards. It is the rhythm that demand sets.”",id:"note-258-takt-target-push",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/258-takt-target-push.jpg?v=36203d2e9b"},{q:"“In most value streams the work itself is fast. It is the waiting between the steps that makes the order late.”",id:"note-259-most-value-streams",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/259-most-value-streams.jpg?v=4c6966eadf"},{q:"“A key point without a reason is a rule people will drop on the first busy day.”",id:"note-260-key-point-without",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/260-key-point-without.jpg?v=eecf9ce7d8"},{q:"“If the problem does not fit on one A3, you have not understood it yet. You have only collected it.”",id:"note-261-if-problem-fit",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/261-if-problem-fit.jpg?v=0e058609cc"},{q:"“An improvement idea that waits three months for an answer teaches the team to stop having ideas.”",id:"note-262-improvement-idea-waits",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/262-improvement-idea-waits.jpg?v=60f0f9a3d9"},{q:"“A kaizen event is not proven on the last day of the workshop. It is proven at the 30-day check, when nobody is watching any more.”",id:"note-263-kaizen-event-proven",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/263-kaizen-event-proven.jpg?v=b90c678133"},{q:"“A near miss is a free lesson. The next one may come with the bill.”",id:"note-264-near-miss-free",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/264-near-miss-free.jpg?v=6c3719689a"},{q:"“A red tag is not a punishment for the object. It is a question: does this still earn its place here?”",id:"note-265-red-tag-punishment",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/265-red-tag-punishment.jpg?v=51c421e4d3"},{q:"“Occupancy can be high and the night can still lose money. RevPAR tells you whether the rooms earned what they could.”",id:"note-266-occupancy-high-night",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/266-occupancy-high-night.jpg?v=9fa84bc6fa"},{q:"“The night audit is where the day's promises meet the day's postings. Every gap found at night is cheaper than one found by the guest.”",id:"note-267-night-audit-where",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/267-night-audit-where.jpg?v=ab191b3ddb"},{q:"“Lost property is a small register with a big promise: what a guest forgot, we did not.”",id:"note-268-lost-property-small",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/268-lost-property-small.jpg?v=aa163d09ca"},{q:"“A huddle that only reads out yesterday's numbers is a report. A huddle that decides today's one action is management.”",id:"note-269-huddle-only-reads",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/269-huddle-only-reads.jpg?v=fc3f992d75"},{q:"“A weekly report should end with a decision, not a summary. Otherwise it was written to be filed, not read.”",id:"note-270-weekly-report-should",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/270-weekly-report-should.jpg?v=566b95df72"},{q:"“Ten projects in progress is often zero projects finished. A portfolio shows you which one to stop.”",id:"note-271-ten-projects-progress",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/271-ten-projects-progress.jpg?v=3c5a2fbec6"},{q:"“A process can be in control and still not be capable. Stable and good enough are two different questions.”",id:"note-272-process-control-still",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/272-process-control-still.jpg?v=bd7074b5f2"},{q:"“A CV is not a list of the jobs you had. It is the proof of the problems you solved.”",id:"note-273-cv-list-jobs",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/273-cv-list-jobs.jpg?v=d7f0970aa9"},{q:"“A cover letter that could be sent to any company will be read by none.”",id:"note-274-cover-letter-could",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/274-cover-letter-could.jpg?v=37fe06cfee"},{q:"“When a process works only because people keep fixing it, the process is not working. The people are.”",id:"note-275-when-process-works",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/275-when-process-works.jpg?v=fddce8ed3c"},{q:"“Fixing fast is not learning fast. The same repair twice is the same mistake twice.”",id:"note-276-fixing-fast-learning",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/276-fixing-fast-learning.jpg?v=ebb297b03a"},{q:"“A workaround is a message from the floor. Punish it and the message stops. The problem does not.”",id:"note-277-workaround-message-from",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/277-workaround-message-from.jpg?v=fdfd21ba4f"},{q:"“The colleague who always knows is not a solution. They are a dependency nobody wrote down.”",id:"note-278-colleague-who-always",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/278-colleague-who-always.jpg?v=232f909c59"},{q:"“The same person called lazy here becomes a model employee abroad. What changed was not the person. It was the system.”",id:"note-279-same-person-called",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/279-same-person-called.jpg?v=e6616eacff"},{q:"“Blaming the laziness of a people is the easiest alibi a failed management can find.”",id:"note-280-blaming-laziness-people",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/280-blaming-laziness-people.jpg?v=bac118efe0"},{q:"“If your emergency is my duty at midnight, my pay is not a question for office hours.”",id:"note-281-if-your-emergency",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/281-if-your-emergency.jpg?v=c6419e8b37"},{q:"“A wage buys your work, not your time off. A phone that must always be on is unpaid work.”",id:"note-282-wage-buys-your",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/282-wage-buys-your.jpg?v=7f68ac07b6"},{q:"“Two days of training is not onboarding. It is an ultimatum with a smile.”",id:"note-283-two-days-training",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/283-two-days-training.jpg?v=a2729316a9"},{q:"“When a shop runs on the owner's memory, every new person is set up to fail.”",id:"note-284-when-shop-runs",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/284-when-shop-runs.jpg?v=49bced5a5a"},{q:"“Paying wages is not charity. It is the contract the owner signed when they hired someone.”",id:"note-285-paying-wages-charity",d:"25 October 2026",iso:"2026-10-25",img:"/media/notes/en/285-paying-wages-charity.jpg?v=6d325e317b"},{q:"“Where everything is urgent, nothing is important. Constant hurry is the most comfortable disguise for a lack of planning.”",id:"note-286-everything-urgent-nothing",d:"1 November 2026",iso:"2026-11-01",img:"/media/notes/en/286-everything-urgent-nothing.jpg?v=88b158f608"},{q:"“Hunting for the culprit is not justice. When punishment replaces root-cause analysis, the same failure is already booked for tomorrow.”",id:"note-287-hunting-culprit-not",d:"1 November 2026",iso:"2026-11-01",img:"/media/notes/en/287-hunting-culprit-not.jpg?v=ba91c41cef"},{q:"“In the face of open injustice there is no neutrality. Silence is not peace. It is a quiet vote for the one doing the trampling.”",id:"note-288-silence-not-peace",d:"1 November 2026",iso:"2026-11-01",img:"/media/notes/en/288-silence-not-peace.jpg?v=982608e66c"},{q:"“A cost does not vanish because the company stopped paying it. It changes department and lands on someone who was not in the room.”",id:"note-289-cost-does-not",d:"1 November 2026",iso:"2026-11-01",img:"/media/notes/en/289-cost-does-not.jpg?v=31143265bf"},{q:"“A manager owes no loyalty to every decision already taken. Only to the best decision possible with the truth in front of them today.”",id:"note-290-loyal-best-decision",d:"1 November 2026",iso:"2026-11-01",img:"/media/notes/en/290-loyal-best-decision.jpg?v=6db1545508"},{q:"“Your value is not how irreplaceable you make yourself by hiding knowledge. It is how independent you make the people around you.”",id:"note-291-hiding-knowledge-value",d:"1 November 2026",iso:"2026-11-01",img:"/media/notes/en/291-hiding-knowledge-value.jpg?v=808394a71b"},{q:"“Power can force people to give you answers. It cannot force them to tell you the truth if you have taught them to fear it.”",id:"note-292-power-forces-answers",d:"1 November 2026",iso:"2026-11-01",img:"/media/notes/en/292-power-forces-answers.jpg?v=494a846a9f"},{q:"“A green report proves the target was reached. It does not prove the way it was reached was right. Ask what had to go unseen.”",id:"note-293-green-report-proves",d:"1 November 2026",iso:"2026-11-01",img:"/media/notes/en/293-green-report-proves.jpg?v=88bb8981a2"},{q:"“A problem does not become everyone's responsibility just because everyone discussed it. A meeting without an owner leaves the decision an orphan.”",id:"note-294-problem-discussed-many",d:"1 November 2026",iso:"2026-11-01",img:"/media/notes/en/294-problem-discussed-many.jpg?v=b9d85c7b88"},{q:"“A machine can save an hour. Only a person decides whether that hour becomes more value, more freedom or simply more work.”",id:"note-295-machine-saves-hour",d:"1 November 2026",iso:"2026-11-01",img:"/media/notes/en/295-machine-saves-hour.jpg?v=dbce857f43"},{q:"“When those who decide are shielded from the consequences, error is no longer a possibility. It is a guarantee.”",id:"note-296-shielded-from-consequences",d:"1 November 2026",iso:"2026-11-01",img:"/media/notes/en/296-shielded-from-consequences.jpg?v=e66f1150cb"},{q:"“A manager who cannot build cooperation through process builds clans through intrigue. A divided team never has time to see the emptiness at the top.”",id:"note-297-divided-team-never",d:"1 November 2026",iso:"2026-11-01",img:"/media/notes/en/297-divided-team-never.jpg?v=ffd6a6326c"},{q:"“Five words test a manager's character: I gave the wrong order. Said in front of the people, not hidden behind them.”",id:"note-298-wrong-order-stand",d:"1 November 2026",iso:"2026-11-01",img:"/media/notes/en/298-wrong-order-stand.jpg?v=0b4bf51d5b"},{q:"“The moral test of a professional is not taken in front of applause. It is taken alone on the floor, where the easy compromise tempts you every second.”",id:"note-299-moral-test-floor",d:"1 November 2026",iso:"2026-11-01",img:"/media/notes/en/299-moral-test-floor.jpg?v=cd24c28682"},{q:"“Injustice does not only begin when someone is given less. Sometimes it begins when far more is asked of them, while everyone insists nobody was treated differently.”",id:"note-300-injustice-asking-more",d:"1 November 2026",iso:"2026-11-01",img:"/media/notes/en/300-injustice-asking-more.jpg?v=865db2a787"},{q:"“Rules that stop at the manager's door no longer protect the organisation from arbitrariness. They protect the manager's arbitrariness from the organisation.”",id:"note-301-rules-manager-door",d:"1 November 2026",iso:"2026-11-01",img:"/media/notes/en/301-rules-manager-door.jpg?v=d1b6f725d6"},{q:"“Someone who can never say no is not loyal. They simply have no boundaries, and where a person's boundaries end, exploitation begins.”",id:"note-302-never-saying-no",d:"1 November 2026",iso:"2026-11-01",img:"/media/notes/en/302-never-saying-no.jpg?v=7ed0455ef2"},{q:"“The saddest success is the one built with such devotion that, when you finally look up, part of the life it was meant to fill has passed without you.”",id:"note-303-saddest-success-built",d:"1 November 2026",iso:"2026-11-01",img:"/media/notes/en/303-saddest-success-built.jpg?v=edb0eb61ab"},{q:"“The hardest glory in operations is a result nobody notices, because nothing had to go wrong to make your work visible.”",id:"note-304-glory-nothing-went",d:"1 November 2026",iso:"2026-11-01",img:"/media/notes/en/304-glory-nothing-went.jpg?v=21e3342309"},{q:"“An organisation can mistake for years its stability for one person's ability to cover everyone else's weaknesses. That is not strength. It is a failure quietly accepted.”",id:"note-305-stability-one-person",d:"1 November 2026",iso:"2026-11-01",img:"/media/notes/en/305-stability-one-person.jpg?v=f6ab61a9ed"},{q:"“The manager who does not know the truth often made it so, decision after decision, by declaring the truth the enemy of their office.”",id:"note-306-truth-enemy-office",d:"1 November 2026",iso:"2026-11-01",img:"/media/notes/en/306-truth-enemy-office.jpg?v=130a910878"},{q:"“When HR stops defending the standard and starts stamping the arbitrary, it is no longer a management function. It is an accomplice.”",id:"note-307-hr-notary-arbitrary",d:"1 November 2026",iso:"2026-11-01",img:"/media/notes/en/307-hr-notary-arbitrary.jpg?v=1381357862"},{q:"“An owner who fights to outdo their own staff in knowledge, authority and ego is not defending the company. They are destroying their own investment.”",id:"note-308-owner-outdo-staff",d:"1 November 2026",iso:"2026-11-01",img:"/media/notes/en/308-owner-outdo-staff.jpg?v=efb26809b5"},{q:"“You cannot pour poison into the village well every day and then wonder with the neighbours why the water makes the children sick.”",id:"note-309-poison-village-well",d:"1 November 2026",iso:"2026-11-01",img:"/media/notes/en/309-poison-village-well.jpg?v=d9deca6ded"},{q:"“Rules show where our responsibility ends. Within them, judgement shows how seriously we take the person. A rulebook must not close the conscience of the one applying it.”",id:"note-310-rules-judgement-person",d:"1 November 2026",iso:"2026-11-01",img:"/media/notes/en/310-rules-judgement-person.jpg?v=c7843dc1d1"},{q:"“A team can break not because of a weak performer, but when everyone learns that keeping one talent means agreeing to be worth less.”",id:"note-311-talent-worth-less",d:"1 November 2026",iso:"2026-11-01",img:"/media/notes/en/311-talent-worth-less.jpg?v=f1ba56f848"},{q:"“Power does not corrupt a person. It pulls back the curtain on what was already there before they sat in the chair.”",id:"note-312-power-pulls-curtain",d:"1 November 2026",iso:"2026-11-01",img:"/media/notes/en/312-power-pulls-curtain.jpg?v=c091ccd583"},{q:"“There is a dangerous comfort in the role of the victim: if everything is someone else's fault, you are excused from acting.”",id:"note-313-comfort-of-victim",d:"1 November 2026",iso:"2026-11-01",img:"/media/notes/en/313-comfort-of-victim.jpg?v=b65014124b"},{q:"“Mistaking chaos for passion and order for sluggishness is the clearest sign of a company that does not know how to judge itself.”",id:"note-314-chaos-for-passion",d:"1 November 2026",iso:"2026-11-01",img:"/media/notes/en/314-chaos-for-passion.jpg?v=6132c106d0"}];